<section class="section page-intro">
  <h1>How value moves through the network</h1>
  <p>A buyer makes one secure Stripe payment. The application creates immutable seller sub-orders and releases each seller share according to its payout policy.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Standard release</h2>
  <p>The seller share becomes eligible after tracked shipment. Platform commission is calculated from the product subtotal at purchase time.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Delivery Guarantee</h2>
  <p>The seller share stays held until buyer confirmation or the protected release date. This is delayed transfer logic, not an escrow service.</p>
</section>
